<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>JWTValidator</PackageId>
    <Title>JWTValidator</Title>
    <Authors>Ollie Rumbol</Authors>
    <Company>JWTValidator.io</Company>
    <Product>JWTValidator</Product>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <Description>A library that simplifies the process of validating JWTs</Description>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/OllieRumbol/ID_Token-JWT_Validator</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>jwt; jwt validator; validation</PackageTags>
    <PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE.txt</PackageLicenseFile>
    <!-- A placeholder for local builds. CI sets the release version from the tag. -->
    <Version>0.0.0-local</Version>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
Changes in 2.0.0, compared with 1.0.3

Breaking changes:
1. .NET 10 only. .NET 6, 7, 8 and 9 are no longer supported.
2. A secret shorter than the minimum for the token's algorithm no longer validates: 32 bytes for HS256, 48 for HS384 and 64 for HS512.
3. WhenDoesJWTExpire returns UTC, not local time. HasJWTExpired gives the correct result in every time zone.
4. IsEmpty returns true for an empty or null dictionary.
5. The library no longer turns on personal-data logging (IdentityModelEventSource.ShowPII). An application that wants it turns it on itself.
6. The package now depends on version 8 of the Microsoft IdentityModel packages, not version 6. This can affect applications that also use those packages directly.

Other changes:
- With lifetime validation on, a token whose exp is after 19 January 2038 now validates. Version 1.0.3 rejected it.
- The dictionary extension methods no longer throw for a null dictionary, or for a null value inside a list.
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://ollierumbol.github.io/JWTValidator</PackageProjectUrl>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="icon.png">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
    <None Include="..\..\LICENSE.txt">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Lets the tests use the internal constructors. No other assembly sees the internals. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="JWTValidatorTests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.IdentityModel.Protocols" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.IdentityModel.Protocols.OpenIdConnect" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.IdentityModel.Tokens.Jwt" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
